  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "As it is right now, the bio section is HUMONGOUS. Especially if the person doesn't have a bio, it's just a gigantic blank empty space, with the \"Current Map\" shoved in to the corner.\nIt just looks like a huge chunk of the UI is missing. Even if someone has a decently long bio to fill up the empty space, why is it still so huge? Why not make it smaller with the ability to scroll?\nWhen I click on someone on my friends list, the thing I immediately want to know first is what map/instance they're currently in. Now \"Current Map\", which is the most important thing, is extremely small and shoved in a corner. I don't want to read someone's entire bio as the first thing I see.",
